24676:
Displacing the block down by x adds buoyant force \rho A x g opposing the motion, so the restoring force is F = -\rho A x g
This is SHM with spring constant k = \rho A g, giving T = 2 \pi \sqrt{M / k}
Hence T = 2 \pi \sqrt{M / (\rho A g)} → (A)

24693:
Magnetic flux is energy / current, giving M L^2 T^{-2} A^{-1}, and self inductance is flux / current, giving M L^2 T^{-2} A^{-2}
Permeability is M L T^{-2} A^{-2} while vector potential is flux / length, giving M L T^{-2} A^{-1}
Hence A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV → (C)

24704:
Only counter ions ionize, so free \text{SO}_4^{2-} comes solely from [\text{Co}(\text{NH}_3)_5\text{Br}]\text{SO}_4 while the other complex releases only \text{Br}^{-}
Moles of free \text{SO}_4^{2-} in 2 L = 0.4 \times \frac{2}{4} = 0.2
Each mole of \text{SO}_4^{2-} gives one mole of \text{BaSO}_4, so 0.2 mol of precipitate forms → (A)

