\Delta E_a = 10 kJ/mol and 2.303 RT = 5.74 kJ/mol, so the ratio = \frac{10}{5.74} = 1.741
The logarithm of the rate-constant ratio is 1.741 → (A)

24721:
In each oxidation the dichromate half-reaction is \text{Cr}_2\text{O}_7^{2-} + 14\text{H}^{+} + 6e^{-} \rightarrow 2\text{Cr}^{3+} + 7\text{H}_2\text{O}
One mole of oxidizing agent takes up 6 electrons in both cases, so X = 6 and Y = 6
X + Y = 6 + 6 = 12 → (12)

